1
00:00:07,360 --> 00:00:12,780
Very well, Lord Ains,
I will take my leave now.

2
00:00:13,110 --> 00:00:18,910
Outstanding work. Keep the first floor
of Nazarick safe until we return.

3
00:00:18,910 --> 00:00:20,660
As you wish.

4
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:22,040
Gate.

5
00:00:28,420 --> 00:00:31,960
I apologize for the place
being so run-down, Lord Ains.

6
00:00:31,960 --> 00:00:35,680
I was in a rush to get it ready
when I heard that you would be coming.

7
00:00:36,390 --> 00:00:38,550
There is no need to be concerned.

8
00:00:39,180 --> 00:00:42,390
You built this place for me,

9
00:00:42,730 --> 00:00:45,730
so it is on par with even Nazarick.

10
00:00:45,730 --> 00:00:46,770
Right!

11
00:00:47,060 --> 00:00:50,520
Still, Aura, tell me one thing--

12
00:00:50,520 --> 00:00:51,750
what is that?

13
00:00:52,610 --> 00:00:56,570
Plain though it may be,
we prepared a throne for you.

14
00:00:57,320 --> 00:00:59,160
What kind of bones are those?

15
00:00:59,160 --> 00:01:00,950
Various different animals.

16
00:01:00,950 --> 00:01:04,290
We assembled the best parts
of griffons, wyverns, and the like.

17
00:01:04,580 --> 00:01:06,040
That's not what...

18
00:01:07,210 --> 00:01:08,540
I see.

19
00:01:08,960 --> 00:01:12,000
I don't care how you look at it,
those appear to be human bones, too!

20
00:01:12,000 --> 00:01:13,670
I'm supposed to sit on <i>that</i>?

21
00:01:14,840 --> 00:01:16,140
Shalltear...

22
00:01:17,430 --> 00:01:20,930
I promised you I would give you
your punishment, right?

23
00:01:20,930 --> 00:01:23,680
This is the perfect time.
I will give it to you now.

24
00:01:24,180 --> 00:01:26,970
Yes, your humiliation.

25
00:01:30,690 --> 00:01:33,860
Indeed! Brilliant!

26
00:01:35,360 --> 00:01:38,610
Sorry, Demiurge. This is the way it is.

27
00:01:38,610 --> 00:01:40,570
Seating yourself on a guardian?

28
00:01:40,570 --> 00:01:43,370
Truly, such is a seat
worthy of the Supreme One,

29
00:01:43,370 --> 00:01:46,460
which is to say,
one which no other could claim!

30
00:01:46,460 --> 00:01:49,880
Leave it to you, Lord Ains.
I never even thought of this!

31
00:01:49,880 --> 00:01:51,460
O-Oh, no?

32
00:01:53,170 --> 00:01:57,300
Lord Ains, may I be excused
from the room for a moment?

33
00:01:57,300 --> 00:01:59,220
I will return at once.

34
00:01:59,220 --> 00:02:01,930
Hmm, well, all right. Go on.

35
00:02:01,930 --> 00:02:03,820
Thank you very much.

36
00:02:21,030 --> 00:02:23,410
I am back, Lord Ains.

37
00:02:23,410 --> 00:02:24,870
Uh, mm-hmm.

38
00:02:25,080 --> 00:02:30,250
Ah yes, Aura, when I left the room,
I bumped into the wall by mistake.

39
00:02:30,250 --> 00:02:33,790
It appears to have been damaged.
Could you fix it up later for me?

40
00:02:33,790 --> 00:02:34,880
I'm sorry about that.

41
00:02:35,920 --> 00:02:37,130
Okay.

42
00:02:40,880 --> 00:02:43,010
Shalltear, is this too hard on you?

43
00:02:43,470 --> 00:02:45,640
--If so--
--It is not hard on me at all!

44
00:02:45,640 --> 00:02:48,180
On the contrary, I take it as a reward!

45
00:02:50,350 --> 00:02:53,690
No, this is the punishment
I gave to Shalltear.

46
00:02:56,400 --> 00:03:00,530
Besides, Shalltear's slip-up
came about due to my failure.

47
00:03:00,530 --> 00:03:03,950
Which means that suffering
through my desire to get out of this

48
00:03:03,950 --> 00:03:05,450
is my punishment to myself.

49
00:03:05,780 --> 00:03:10,790
Still, Peroroncino, just how kinky
did you configure her to be?!

50
00:04:42,920 --> 00:04:45,510
All right, down to business.

51
00:04:46,220 --> 00:04:48,970
Do you think we did
a decent job of alarming them?

52
00:04:48,970 --> 00:04:51,520
I think it was perfect, Lord Ains.

53
00:04:51,850 --> 00:04:56,270
Absolutely. Did you see
those Lizard Men's faces?

54
00:04:56,690 --> 00:05:00,400
I see. Then I suppose the first stage

55
00:05:00,400 --> 00:05:05,240
of the demonstration that Cocytus
hoped for was successful enough.

56
00:05:05,240 --> 00:05:06,280
Now...

57
00:05:06,530 --> 00:05:09,350
...how about a look at
what the Lizard Men are up to?

58
00:05:16,750 --> 00:05:18,380
They're wasting their efforts.

59
00:05:20,000 --> 00:05:21,950
Those would be the chiefs.

60
00:05:22,800 --> 00:05:26,760
Hmm? The white one and the one
with the magic weapon aren't there.

61
00:05:28,800 --> 00:05:31,140
Zaryusu was his name, wasn't it?

62
00:05:31,140 --> 00:05:34,060
Ah, yes. That was his name.

63
00:05:34,060 --> 00:05:36,270
Maybe he's inside one of the houses.

64
00:05:36,480 --> 00:05:37,700
He could be.

65
00:05:41,730 --> 00:05:46,940
Normally, the Mirror of Remote Viewing
can't offer a view indoors.

66
00:05:47,320 --> 00:05:50,620
However, using magic,
I can create a sensory organ,

67
00:05:50,620 --> 00:05:52,660
then by linking the two, I can...

68
00:06:00,750 --> 00:06:01,460
No!

69
00:06:04,420 --> 00:06:06,170
--What unpleasant creatures!
--Ugh...

70
00:06:06,170 --> 00:06:09,590
--U-Um, I, er...
--Cocytus is just about to attack them!

71
00:06:09,590 --> 00:06:12,140
--They should be given a punishment!
--Right! Absolutely right!

72
00:06:12,140 --> 00:06:14,180
They really are rude, aren't they?!

73
00:06:14,180 --> 00:06:16,600
Um... I, uh...

74
00:06:16,600 --> 00:06:18,480
I'm so jealous...

75
00:06:20,690 --> 00:06:25,480
Well, they <i>are</i> about to die.
I've seen in movies that in these situations,

76
00:06:25,480 --> 00:06:29,950
the instinct to preserve the species kicks in,
or something. Mm-hmm.

77
00:06:29,950 --> 00:06:33,030
--That is exactly correct!
--Yes, this much can be forgiven.

78
00:06:33,030 --> 00:06:34,370
--Absolutely, absolutely!
--Yes, this much can be forgiven.

79
00:06:34,370 --> 00:06:36,500
--You are right, Lord Ains!
--U-Uh, that is, um...

80
00:06:36,500 --> 00:06:39,500
--I wish Lord Ains and I could--
--All of you, be quiet!

81
00:06:41,750 --> 00:06:44,130
Somehow, the wind
has gone out of my sails now...

82
00:06:44,880 --> 00:06:48,300
Oh, crap! That was too soon for Aura and Mare!

83
00:06:48,300 --> 00:06:51,680
What am I going to tell them
when they ask where babies come from?!

84
00:06:52,050 --> 00:06:54,430
Turn to Albedo? Ugh, out of the question.

85
00:06:55,510 --> 00:06:59,810
Demiurge? He can probably
explain it clinically. He's in the running.

86
00:07:00,310 --> 00:07:04,650
Shalltear? Hmm, that doesn't actually
sound as bad as I would have expected.

87
00:07:04,900 --> 00:07:07,620
Whatever the case,
it's a problem for a later date.

88
00:07:08,610 --> 00:07:12,700
Ahem, Aura, since there has been
no activity at this stage,

89
00:07:12,700 --> 00:07:15,030
the chances of coming into contact

90
00:07:15,030 --> 00:07:19,160
with the one who used the world item
on Shalltear seem extremely low,

91
00:07:19,160 --> 00:07:21,500
but remain vigilant to your surroundings.

92
00:07:21,500 --> 00:07:22,310
Right!

93
00:07:22,790 --> 00:07:26,800
If there is an Yggdrasil player
on the Lizard Men's side,

94
00:07:26,800 --> 00:07:31,800
and they won't ally with us,
we must destroy them with our full force,

95
00:07:31,800 --> 00:07:34,350
to keep any information from getting out.

96
00:08:15,340 --> 00:08:18,280
Are you telling me <i>that</i> is Cocytus?

97
00:08:22,890 --> 00:08:30,440
All right, Lord Ains is watching on, as well.
Show us your brilliance.

98
00:08:31,400 --> 00:08:33,200
But before we start...

99
00:08:33,570 --> 00:08:35,110
Ice Pillars!

100
00:08:36,070 --> 00:08:38,950
As warriors who have the resolve to come here,

101
00:08:38,950 --> 00:08:42,710
pardon the affront,
but I must make an announcement.

102
00:08:42,710 --> 00:08:45,000
On this side of that gate is your destruction.

103
00:08:45,000 --> 00:08:49,020
Know that if you advance
beyond there, death awaits you.

104
00:08:50,590 --> 00:08:53,720
Hey, man, this guy's
surprisingly nice, isn't he?

105
00:08:58,550 --> 00:09:02,100
You all stay there--no, return to the village.

106
00:09:02,100 --> 00:09:04,980
Wha--?! No, let us fight with you!

107
00:09:05,890 --> 00:09:09,190
It is not cowardly to withdraw! Nor is living!

108
00:09:09,190 --> 00:09:10,110
Then--

109
00:09:10,110 --> 00:09:12,360
But there are some of us
Lizard Men who cannot retreat!

110
00:09:12,360 --> 00:09:14,700
You would not accept the rule of those of us

111
00:09:14,700 --> 00:09:17,870
who stand as chiefs
if we did not fight, would you?!

112
00:09:18,030 --> 00:09:21,120
But Chief, we're here to fight!

113
00:09:21,990 --> 00:09:26,920
You youngsters go home.
This is a job for us older warriors.

114
00:09:26,920 --> 00:09:27,620
Hmm.

115
00:09:30,840 --> 00:09:33,260
Sorry to keep you, Cocytus!

116
00:09:35,970 --> 00:09:38,680
Charge!

117
00:09:41,760 --> 00:09:47,100
I hate to do this to warriors,
but I must first reduce your numbers.

118
00:09:47,980 --> 00:09:49,720
Frost Aura!

119
00:10:01,700 --> 00:10:04,910
Hmm, seems about right.

120
00:10:15,510 --> 00:10:19,890
Those of us who are guardian class
have all acquired items and so forth

121
00:10:19,890 --> 00:10:22,390
that grant us resistance to ranged weapons.

122
00:10:28,640 --> 00:10:30,850
God Slaying Emperor Blade!

123
00:10:35,070 --> 00:10:38,240
Martial Art, Iron Natural Weapon!

124
00:10:39,030 --> 00:10:40,490
Iron Skin!

125
00:10:47,330 --> 00:10:51,290
Hmm, yes indeed. Not a bad sword.

126
00:10:52,960 --> 00:10:54,250
Tch!

127
00:10:56,090 --> 00:10:57,510
You're in the way.

128
00:11:00,220 --> 00:11:04,390
Over Magic! Mass Slight Cure Wounds!

129
00:11:17,940 --> 00:11:19,990
You still have the will to fight?

130
00:11:19,990 --> 00:11:22,230
Then I will return this to you.

131
00:11:30,410 --> 00:11:34,540
That is getting annoying. Piercing Icicles!

132
00:11:56,900 --> 00:12:02,490
Now then, there are two of you left?
Lord Ains said as much,

133
00:12:02,490 --> 00:12:05,740
and sure enough, you two lasted until the end.

134
00:12:05,910 --> 00:12:08,490
My brother, how hurt are you?

135
00:12:08,660 --> 00:12:12,120
Badly. The pain is still throbbing.

136
00:12:12,120 --> 00:12:14,750
Even so, I can swing my sword
a few more times.

137
00:12:14,750 --> 00:12:18,460
You can? Then that will be enough.

138
00:12:18,460 --> 00:12:22,010
The truth is, I am just about
out of magic power.

139
00:12:22,010 --> 00:12:23,880
If I don't watch out,
I could collapse right here.

140
00:12:24,050 --> 00:12:29,890
Is that right? Brother, you push yourself
too hard. But, all the same,

141
00:12:30,060 --> 00:12:36,020
I will continue to swing my sword,
right up until the last moment!

142
00:12:36,730 --> 00:12:38,730
A fine battle cry.

143
00:12:38,980 --> 00:12:44,320
Outstanding, my brother! You're right!
Let's fight until the very end!

144
00:12:45,110 --> 00:12:48,740
Now, let's not keep you waiting, Sir Cocytus!

145
00:12:48,740 --> 00:12:50,660
It is no matter to me.

146
00:12:50,660 --> 00:12:54,500
I am not so boorish as to
come between brothers saying farewell.

147
00:12:54,500 --> 00:12:57,540
Prepare yourselves--no, I beg your pardon.

148
00:12:57,540 --> 00:13:00,460
You had already prepared yourselves
before we even began.

149
00:13:01,670 --> 00:13:03,740
Allow me to formally ask your names.

150
00:13:04,430 --> 00:13:06,510
Shasuryu Shasha.

151
00:13:06,760 --> 00:13:08,760
Zaryusu Shasha.

152
00:13:09,100 --> 00:13:14,230
I shall remember them as the names of warriors.

153
00:13:15,310 --> 00:13:18,310
Also, allow me to apologize in advance.

154
00:13:18,310 --> 00:13:23,240
Normally, I would face you
with weapons in each hand,

155
00:13:23,240 --> 00:13:27,030
but you are not mighty enough
for me to draw both.

156
00:13:27,360 --> 00:13:29,160
That's a shame.

157
00:13:29,160 --> 00:13:32,330
It sure is. Here goes!

158
00:13:32,700 --> 00:13:35,080
Earth Bind!

159
00:13:35,620 --> 00:13:38,630
My defense cannot be penetrated by one

160
00:13:38,630 --> 00:13:41,750
whose magic level is inferior to mine!

161
00:13:41,750 --> 00:13:44,050
Icy Burst!

162
00:13:56,810 --> 00:13:58,810
If you wish to take me by surprise,

163
00:13:59,610 --> 00:14:02,040
you should do it quietly!

164
00:14:06,700 --> 00:14:07,790
Blood?

165
00:14:08,280 --> 00:14:10,660
All of that, for <i>this</i>?

166
00:14:12,870 --> 00:14:15,040
Magnificent.

167
00:14:17,460 --> 00:14:21,920
I'm sorry, but I have a skill
that temporarily negates attacks

168
00:14:21,920 --> 00:14:26,800
by weapons with weak magic power.
As long as it is activated,

169
00:14:26,800 --> 00:14:29,550
your attacks are meaningless.

170
00:14:32,510 --> 00:14:33,760
However...!

171
00:14:39,940 --> 00:14:43,400
Cocytus, you fought admirably.

172
00:14:43,650 --> 00:14:45,690
Thank you very much.

173
00:14:45,690 --> 00:14:49,410
That being said, what you gave them
this time was the stick.

174
00:14:49,410 --> 00:14:52,530
From here on,
what you must give them is the carrot.

175
00:14:52,530 --> 00:14:55,410
It must not be a reign of terror.

176
00:14:55,620 --> 00:14:57,540
I understand.

177
00:14:57,750 --> 00:15:02,040
Very good. Listen to me, guardians.

178
00:15:02,040 --> 00:15:06,260
The rule over the Lizard Men villages
is assigned to Cocytus.

179
00:15:06,260 --> 00:15:10,130
If ever Cocytus requests
your support, assist him.

180
00:15:10,130 --> 00:15:15,310
Lord Ains, what is to be
the disposition of those Lizard Men?

181
00:15:15,470 --> 00:15:17,390
Those Lizard Men...?

182
00:15:17,390 --> 00:15:22,520
Yes. The one called Zaryusu,
and the one called Shasuryu.

183
00:15:22,520 --> 00:15:25,860
Ah, yes. Let's recover their bodies,

184
00:15:25,860 --> 00:15:29,030
and use them as subjects
in the creation of undead

185
00:15:29,030 --> 00:15:31,070
that do not rely on my skill.

186
00:15:31,070 --> 00:15:33,160
I believe we can do better.

187
00:15:33,160 --> 00:15:35,200
Hmm? What do you mean?

188
00:15:35,200 --> 00:15:38,200
While they were weaklings,
I also saw in them the brilliance of warriors

189
00:15:38,200 --> 00:15:41,460
who did not balk at someone
stronger than themselves.

190
00:15:41,670 --> 00:15:47,210
I believe they have the potential
to become stronger than we assume.

191
00:15:47,210 --> 00:15:52,220
Lord Ains, you have not conducted
any experiments in raising the dead.

192
00:15:52,760 --> 00:15:55,220
What if you were to use them for that?

193
00:15:55,470 --> 00:15:58,630
The brilliance of warriors, he calls it?

194
00:16:00,020 --> 00:16:03,770
I see. They're too precious to pass up, then?

195
00:16:03,770 --> 00:16:07,230
Is there anyone who can
represent the Lizard Men villages?

196
00:16:07,230 --> 00:16:09,860
There was one white Lizard Man
with druidic powers,

197
00:16:09,860 --> 00:16:13,610
who did not participate in the fighting.

198
00:16:13,610 --> 00:16:15,610
<i>That</i> one? You don't say.

199
00:16:16,660 --> 00:16:20,870
All right, how long will it take
to bring her here?

200
00:16:20,870 --> 00:16:24,080
Forgive me, but assuming you would ask that,

201
00:16:24,080 --> 00:16:26,590
I have called her to the next room already.

202
00:16:26,590 --> 00:16:28,250
Ho?

203
00:16:32,420 --> 00:16:37,430
Not at all. Well done, Cocytus.
Your judgment was on the mark.

204
00:16:37,430 --> 00:16:40,060
All right, then, bring her in.

205
00:16:40,060 --> 00:16:40,960
Yes, my lord.

206
00:16:43,560 --> 00:16:44,940
Tell me your name.

207
00:16:45,600 --> 00:16:50,860
Yes, Lord Ains Ooal Gown,
great and supreme king of death.

208
00:16:50,860 --> 00:16:54,280
I am Crusch Lulu,
here on behalf of the Lizard Men.

209
00:16:55,240 --> 00:16:57,620
Mm-hmm, thanks for coming.

210
00:16:57,830 --> 00:17:04,970
Yes, Lord Gown. Please accept
the absolute allegiance of the Lizard Men.

211
00:17:05,420 --> 00:17:06,230
Mm-hmm.

212
00:17:14,050 --> 00:17:17,850
I have a special request for you.

213
00:17:18,180 --> 00:17:22,140
If there is anything that I,
your loyal servant, can do, Lord Gown,

214
00:17:22,140 --> 00:17:23,350
then please ask.

215
00:17:23,980 --> 00:17:26,950
Not as my servant.

216
00:17:27,600 --> 00:17:30,480
In return, I will return Zaryusu to life.

217
00:17:30,690 --> 00:17:32,080
Is that possible...?

218
00:17:32,610 --> 00:17:35,880
I am capable of manipulating
even life and death.

219
00:17:36,410 --> 00:17:41,490
To me, death is nothing more
than a state of being.

220
00:17:41,490 --> 00:17:46,590
Then, what do you desire of me,
your loyal slave?

221
00:17:47,540 --> 00:17:49,500
Is it my body?

222
00:17:52,670 --> 00:17:55,040
No, not exactly...

223
00:17:56,050 --> 00:17:59,680
Ahem. Certainly not. It's simple.

224
00:17:59,680 --> 00:18:02,060
I want you to keep a close watch to make sure

225
00:18:02,060 --> 00:18:04,270
that there are no Lizard Men
who would betray me.

226
00:18:04,600 --> 00:18:07,270
There are no such Lizard Men.

227
00:18:07,270 --> 00:18:11,520
I am not so foolish as to actually believe that.

228
00:18:13,480 --> 00:18:16,240
Right now, you have
a miracle hanging over you.

229
00:18:16,240 --> 00:18:20,700
However, that miracle
will not necessarily last forever.

230
00:18:20,700 --> 00:18:25,290
If you do not seize upon this moment,
it will all come to an end.

231
00:18:26,040 --> 00:18:33,340
Crusch, what is the most important thing
to you? I want you to think about that.

232
00:18:34,050 --> 00:18:38,800
I want you to covertly keep watch
on your fellow Lizard Men from the inside.

233
00:18:39,760 --> 00:18:43,970
I will cast a special magic spell
on Zaryusu when I revive him.

234
00:18:43,970 --> 00:18:46,930
If I determine that you have betrayed me,

235
00:18:46,930 --> 00:18:51,440
the spell will immediately render him dead.
That will bring you grief.

236
00:18:52,110 --> 00:18:57,950
However, it is a small price to pay
to have Zaryusu back, isn't it?

237
00:18:58,280 --> 00:19:00,490
Except that there is no such spell.

238
00:19:08,080 --> 00:19:13,150
Very well, Crusch Lulu, make your choice now.

239
00:19:14,250 --> 00:19:16,750
Even if she declines, do nothing.

240
00:19:18,420 --> 00:19:21,680
Well, what is your answer,

241
00:19:21,680 --> 00:19:23,370
Crusch Lulu?

242
00:19:27,390 --> 00:19:28,600
Zaryusu...

243
00:19:30,020 --> 00:19:31,100
Zaryusu...

244
00:19:32,690 --> 00:19:33,900
Zaryusu...

245
00:19:35,690 --> 00:19:37,110
Zaryusu...

246
00:19:38,320 --> 00:19:39,950
Zaryusu...

